<figure class="session-story">
  <ol class="session-vertical-flow" aria-label="High-level StarCraft II Battle.net session flow">
    <li class="session-stage front-stage">
      <div class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <h3>Front connection</h3>
        <p>The client connects to the regional Front endpoint. TLS protects the
        connection. WebSocket sets the message boundaries. Front carries connection
        and account operations.</p>
        <p class="stage-wire">TCP/1119 → TLS → WebSocket → Front RPC</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="session-stage front-stage">
      <div class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <h3>Account login</h3>
        <p>Front can accept a cached credential. Otherwise, the server sends an HTTPS
        account challenge. A successful logon returns the SC2 game accounts and a
        Front session key.</p>
        <p class="stage-wire">Front logon → optional web challenge → LogonResult</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="session-stage handoff-stage">
      <div class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">03</div>
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <h3>Sunken session data</h3>
        <p>Battle.net can report a selected SC2 game account. The first game-account
        entity from <code>LogonResult</code> is used to call
        <code>GameUtilities.ProcessClientRequest</code>.</p>
        <p>The response contains the private data for Sunken.</p>
        <div class="handoff-material" aria-label="Three essential values returned by the GameUtilities handoff">
          <div><strong>Native endpoint</strong><span>The address for the Sunken connection.</span></div>
          <div><strong>64-byte session seed</strong><span>The input for the Resume proof and transport keys.</span></div>
          <div><strong><code>LogonResponse3</code></strong><span>The identity, region, and bootstrap values.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="session-stage sunken-stage">
      <div class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">04</div>
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <h3>Sunken connection</h3>
        <p>The client opens a new TCP connection to Sunken. The client sends
        <code>Auth/1 ResumeRequest</code>. The proof confirms possession of the
        handoff seed. The proof binds the new connection to the authorized account.</p>
        <p class="connection-switch"><b>This step changes the TCP connection.</b>
        Authorization transfers to Sunken, and Front closes.</p>
        <p class="stage-wire">new TCP/1119 → plaintext Sunken Auth → Resume proof</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="session-stage sunken-stage">
      <div class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">05</div>
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <h3>Protected stream</h3>
        <p>The client must first validate the server proof. The client then sends
        <code>Conn/5 EnableEncryption</code>. This command enables a separate RC4
        state for each direction. The protected Sunken stream carries all native
        services.</p>
        <p class="stage-wire">RC4-protected Sunken → static route table → decoded records</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</figure>
